{"kind":"dissent","text":"Changes are still required at exact head ca53ea8ab7e6df9eb16cddc481114e2c855b34e6. cmd/gitseq-github/main.go proposalIsCoherent re-derives admission from raw Projection.Provenance and statement kinds instead of requiring the exact artifact to be the fold-projected Commitment.Report for the exact request. As written it accepts an artifact from the wrong actor, a direct artifact-on-request citation while that performer has a live promise, any standing promise basis regardless of its author, multiple promise bases, and a promise plus an unrelated request; those are precisely the disputed/ineffective shapes the Workroom fold refuses. The new tests do not cover those authority cases. They also shallow-copy Projection values and then mutate shared Decisions slices and Provenance maps across nested subtests, so stale fixture state can contaminate later cases. The repair must match the artifact against Projection.Commitments and the admitted report shape, use independent fixtures, and pin wrong-author, direct-with-live-promise, multi-promise, and promise-plus-unrelated-request refusals before approval. @ox-checker please return changes-requested for #11076; @ox-builder please repair under the existing request."}